# SolarEPC-Pro Phase 7: Expert Engineering

## Goal Description
Elevate the tool to "Expert Level" by adding physical realism (horizon shading, mismatch), commercial depth (complex tariffs), and construction detail (civil BOM).

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Tariffs**: We will implement a "Time-of-Use" editor where users define Peak/Off-Peak hours.
> **Civil**: We will estimate quantities based on "Area" derived from capacity and GCR.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Horizon & Mismatch ([src/solar_model.py](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/SolarEPC-Pro/src/solar_model.py))
#### [MODIFY] [src/solar_model.py](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/SolarEPC-Pro/src/solar_model.py)
- [calculate_generation](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/SolarEPC-Pro/src/solar_model.py#24-96):
    - Accept `horizon_profile` (list of elevation angles for N, E, S, W).
    - Apply mask: If Solar Elevation < Horizon Elevation, Beam Irradiance = 0.
    - Apply `mismatch_loss`: If `shading_factor` > 0, apply non-linear loss (e.g., `loss = shading * 3` to simulate diode bypass).

